
## Agent directives (strict)
- CRITICAL: SQL only in PostgreSQL dialect.
- CRITICAL: migration files must always be wrapped in a transaction (BEGIN / COMMIT).
- CRITICAL: always warn when uncommitted changes expose secrets or sensitive information.
- CRITICAL: always warn when uncommitted changes introduce SQL injection.
  (omitting it means admin-only; may be intentional but must be explicit).

## Feature-addition order
1. Check application.conf and ConfigurationProvider.kt for active configs.
2. Define model/ (domain entities) and dto/ (API contracts).
3. Persistence in repository/ with Exposed DSL.
4. Business logic in service/ plus tests.
5. Wire HTTP endpoints in route/ and Koin injection in modules/.

